# The fixed core of the Deep Time lite mod set (tools/smoke/lite_set.py): one mod id per line, then why.
# A mod id that no jar of the set provides is skipped with a note (a client-only mod is not on the
# server, a mod the pack dropped is gone). Everything else of the lite set is derived from Deep Time's
# data, never listed here: see lite_set.py's header for the rules.

# Deep Time and its world
deeptime            the mod under test
toroidal_world      the planet wraps through Toroidal World (a required dependency of Deep Time; the pinned bundle of profiles/mic.txt)
distanthorizons     far terrain comes from Deep Time's world data (compat/dh); the pack's pin
deeptime_devmap     the internal developer map (play-client-stage.sh --devmap; never the pack's)

# The pack's router. ClimateMappingBuilder samples the pack's own minecraft:overworld noise settings at a
# world's first start, and MIC's router is Tectonic's (a mixin mod, so lite_set.py's router rule, which
# looks for data overrides, cannot see it). Without it the climate mapping would be vanilla's.
tectonic            Deep Time's climate mapping samples the pack's overworld router (Tectonic's)

# Client performance mods the pack already has (Ben, 2026-10-22: a lighter client). Their required
# companions come from the dependency closure.
sodium              client performance: renderer
lithium             performance: game logic
c2me                performance: chunk loading and generation
modernfix           performance: start-up and memory
ferritecore         performance: memory
immediatelyfast     client performance: immediate-mode rendering
entityculling       client performance: entity culling

# Deep Time's deep seas (Ben, 2026-10-22: vanilla water shows the floor of the deepest sea from the surface).
# Client only; its library MossyLib comes from the dependency closure.
bathymetry@client   deep water darkens with depth seen from above (the pack's pin)

# Undeclared client dependencies, found by booting the lite client (tools/client/vm-client.sh --mods
# mic-lite). "mod@client" keeps a mod in the client set only; the server boots without it.
jei@client          Destroy's DestroyMysteriousItemConversions loads JEI's API on the client and Destroy does not declare JEI (the pack always has it)
